course: dictionary
lesson: 1778
title: Cliffhangers
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A cliffhanger is an ending that leaves you in suspense, which means not knowing what will happen next. Writers and TV makers use it on purpose, stopping at a tense moment so you want to keep reading or watching. «A cliffhanger ends a chapter or episode at a tense moment, so the reader must read on.»
explain: The word also works outside stories. When a contest stays uncertain until the very end, such as a close football match, it is a cliffhanger too.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Words like tense and worry show the mood at the end, and they tell you why the reader feels pulled to go on.
fact: A cliffhanger is a noun: one cliffhanger, two cliffhangers.
fact: «A cliffhanger» means an exciting ending that leaves you not knowing what happens next.
fact: «Cliffhanger» can also mean any contest or situation where the result stays uncertain until the very end.
fact: In writing lessons, a chapter that ends on a cliffhanger tells the reader to keep going.
fact: «Tense» means full of worry or nervous feeling, so a tense moment is a worrying one.
exercise: «A cliffhanger ends a chapter at a tense moment.» What is a cliffhanger? | A word for the last page of a dictionary | *An exciting ending that leaves you wanting to know what happens next | A cake that changes size | A list of all the characters in a book
exercise: The football match stayed level until the final whistle, and every fan was on the edge of their seat. Why might this be called a cliffhanger? | Everyone left early | It ended with a score of zero before half time | *Its result stayed uncertain until the very end | It was played on a cliff
exercise: What do the words «full of hope and worry at once» tell you about a cliffhanger? | The story is funny and light | It is a happy wedding scene | *It makes the reader feel tense and unsure what comes next | It is a list of ingredients
test: Which sentence uses cliffhanger correctly? | My cliffhanger is a red bicycle with a bell. | *The episode ended on a cliffhanger, so we had to watch the next one. | We ate our cliffhanger at the picnic. | The cake was made with three eggs and a cup of flour.
test: A reader says the chapter's ending is a cliffhanger. What do they mean? | The ending is boring and they stopped reading | The chapter is the shortest in the book | *The ending is gripping, so they want to read on | The chapter has no words in it
exam: In «Under the table she finds a little cake marked "EAT ME", reasons that any change of size will help, and eats it all: the part ends on a cliffhanger.», what makes this a cliffhanger? | *The reader does not know what will happen to her after she eats the cake | The cake has a label on it | She finds a table under a tree | The story has finished and everyone is happy
